From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:31:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: add a lab switch for USB3 over USB4
 on T8132

T8132 keeps the PIPE on the dummy backend in CIO mode because USB3
routed to the USB4 side did not train when the CIO mode was added.
Nothing has measured that path on a J604 with a USB4 dock since.

Add t8132_usb4_pipe, off by default. When it is set, a T8132 port in
CIO mode routes its PIPE to the USB4 side as the older SoCs do. The
switch is read at each mode change, so a test can set it and replug a
dock without a reboot. With it off nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index bff097bd1c..cdcc98e1b2 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -1490,16 +1490,28 @@ static bool atcphy_mode_is_cio(enum atcphy_mode mode)
 	return mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_TBT || mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB4;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Lab switch for USB3 tunnelled over USB4 on T8132: route the PIPE to the USB4
+ * side in CIO, as the older SoCs do. Read at each mode change, so it applies
+ * from the next cable connection. Off by default, see atcphy_pipe_state_for().
+ */
+static bool t8132_usb4_pipe;
+module_param(t8132_usb4_pipe, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_usb4_pipe,
+		 "T8132: route the PIPE to the USB4 side in CIO mode for tunnelled USB3 (default: N; experimental)");
+
 /*
  * The PIPE backend a mode needs. T8132 carries no USB3 over USB4 yet, so its
  * PIPE stays on the dummy backend in CIO, as in a mode without USB3. Routed to
  * the USB4 side, the controller's SuperSpeed port keeps detecting a link it
- * cannot train, and the lock handshake on the way back times out.
+ * cannot train, and the lock handshake on the way back times out. The
+ * t8132_usb4_pipe switch routes it there anyway, to test that again.
  */
 static enum atcphy_pipehandler_state
 atcphy_pipe_state_for(const struct apple_atcphy *atcphy, enum atcphy_mode mode)
 {
-	if (atcphy->hw->gen == ATCPHY_GENERATION_T8132 && atcphy_mode_is_cio(mode))
+	if (atcphy->hw->gen == ATCPHY_GENERATION_T8132 && atcphy_mode_is_cio(mode) &&
+	    !READ_ONCE(t8132_usb4_pipe))
 		return ATCPHY_PIPEHANDLER_STATE_DUMMY;
 	return atcphy_modes[mode].pipehandler_state;
 }
